{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790020934,"nonce":"5uwopBcY3tbYGf7Um4Zn+qb04qY=","message":"Designed 2026-09-21 in doc/design/config-entity.md (E1–E11). Refinements over D1 as this task was written, so whoever picks it up builds the right thing:\n\n1. ONE entity, typename config, namespace work — not one per kind. Schema, flows, views and rules are sections of it (E1).\n2. Two wire ops, SetEntry{path, value JSON} and RemoveEntry{path} (prefix remove), plus a payload-less Create. The typed vocabulary (DefineField, AddEnumValue, …) is the Go API on ConfigCache emitting those two on well-known paths: fields/\u003ckey\u003e, fields/\u003ckey\u003e/values/\u003cid\u003e, types/\u003cid\u003e, relations/\u003ckey\u003e, flows|views|rules/\u003cname\u003e (E2, E3). op.Validate is structural only and frozen; semantic rules live at write time (E6).\n3. Types carry ordinal, not rank (rank is the 441dcbb field kind) (E4).\n4. Compile = replay in dag order into a flat map; typed projection is lenient and lists orphans in Snapshot.Problems (E5).\n5. ConfigCache.Update(fn) computes the changes INSIDE the write lock against the re-read entity, one pack, one commit — so an import is atomic and reconcile diffs against reality (E6).\n6. No entity = embedded base preset (status open/closed, freeform labels), never written; RepoCache.Schema() hides the difference (E7). Status field carries on_open/on_close for the D3 SetStatusOp shim.\n7. Singleton = lowest create lamport then lowest id; duplicates reported, init refuses when one exists (E8).\n8. Commands: schema [init|export|import|log|rm]; YAML via goccy/go-yaml (E11).\nPackage layout: entities/config, schema/ (types, presets, reconcile), cache/config_*.go, commands/schema.","files":null}]}